.TH AR 4
.SH NAME
ar \- archive (library) file format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <ar.h>"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The archive command
.BR ar (1)
is used to combine several files into one.
Archives are used mainly as libraries to be searched by the link-editor
.BR ld (1).
.PP
A file produced by
\fBar\fR has a magic number at the start, followed by the constituent files, each preceded by a file header. The magic number and header layout as described in the include file are:
.nf
#define ARMAG   "!<arch>\en"
#define SARMAG  8

#define ARFMAG  "`\en"

struct ar_hdr {
        char    ar_name[16];
        char    ar_date[12];
        char    ar_uid[6];
        char    ar_gid[6];
        char    ar_mode[8];
        char    ar_size[10];
        char    ar_fmag[2];
};
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ar(1), ld(1), nm(1)
.sp
